Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:23:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/55] Drone tracks: a drone row's Hz lane kept when its notes
 are recorded, moved or made Euclidean

A drone row's expression X is its Hz lane, not the MPE of its notes (the notes are only the
row's gate). Note edits still treated it as the notes' MPE:

- Recording a note under PLAY + REC (audition pad, MIDI, keyboard, the automation view's
  note editor): InstrumentClip::recordNoteOn() wrote the note's MPE values (0 for a pad) into
  X from the note to the next one, or over the whole lane for the row's only note. The new
  note played at the tone's own pitch and the lane's later nodes were gone (only undoing the
  whole recording brought them back).
- The Euclidean edit (audition pad held, vertical encoder pressed and turned) deleted all
  of X.
- A held note moved to another row (vertical encoder) took the lane's nodes from the note to
  the next one along and put them into the other row: the lane moved with the note, and a
  note moved onto a drone row cleared that row's lane where it landed.

NoteRow::expressionIsHzLane() says which rows these are. recordNoteOn(),
clearMPEUpUntilNextNote(), editNumEuclideanEvents(), the note move in scrollVertical() and
the MPE note editing at a MIDI note-off (reportNoteOffForMPEEditing()) leave such a lane
alone.

Test: mastertune tests/song/drone_edit_emu.py (run.sh DRONE=1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
